{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1554363-the-war-in-ukraine-has-surprising-potential-for-lore","id":1554363,"title":"The War in Ukraine has surprising potential for lore","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-14T10:56:11-07:00","id":1554363,"title":"The War in Ukraine has surprising potential for lore","content":"The Campaign could revolve around defending caerns around Ukraine from Russian trespassers, protecting civilians or fighting Swords of Heimdall that are working with the Wagner Group. The suffering and cruelty of the war could attract all kinds of Banes.<br /> <br /> Maybe there could be a plot revolving around Shinzui Industries or Pentex getting involved in the war.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Russians that trespassed in Chernobyl became Fomori later in the war?<br /> <br /> Maybe the crude oil being burned in the destruction of refineries unintentionally spreads wyrm taint by creating Smog Elementals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  punctuation 10-14-2025, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-14T16:57:07-07:00","id":1554368,"title":"","content":"A big problem with trying to work game lore into an on-going real world conflict is that you don't know what's going to happen; and that's before getting into the issues with how any players might feel about painting real things with fictional brushes.<br /> <br /> There's a lot we don't know that's going to get clearer over time, and what might feel like a good fit now might change with that knowledge. There's a reason a lot of games (even the WoD back in the 90s) used fictional companies and organizations. It's a lot easier to have a Pentex owned PMC group that stands in for the Wagner Group than actually using them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-14T23:27:57-07:00","id":1554371,"title":"","content":"Yeah... it is a loaded gun you shouldn't poke even with a ten foot pole<br /> <i>Ususally</i><br /> BUT if you very carefully talk it through with your group, making sure everyone is okay with it?<br /> It is just like any other conflict happening right now in the world<br /> <br /> Ukraine already had some... no to comfortable place in WoD<br /> Near the Kyiv Necropolis lies the Babi Yar ravine - where one of the largest mass murders of World War II happened - and it is part of the Dark Kingdom of Wire<br /> Ukraine fell under the domain of Baba Yaga, her shadow still lingers, and since the Dark Ages Kyiv was ruled by Darvag Grozny, the Terrible; the Butcher of Rus, a Tzimisce of considerable powers, who had had a grudge against christianity, and protected the city from the ravages of all other Cainites but not out of loyalty to Kyiv, but because he wanted to destroy the city himself.<br /> ...and he offered sacrifices in blood to the &quot;little grandmother&quot; Baba Yaga; after she &quot;died&quot;, Grozny entered Torpor and his brood joined the Sabbat<br /> On werewolf front all the above and the oil pipes, Chernobyl, and similar things already made the area a headache<br /> <br /> Does it have lore and story potential?<br /> Yes<br /> Do you have to treat it very carefully?<br /> Yes<br /> Does it fundamentally different than any other conflict in the area or those conflicts already happening in the world?<br /> Not that much, maybe the presence of the Babi Yar ravine and Chernobyl and the fact that would make it a bit different place (and harder situations) it was the domain of a really monstorus Tzimisce and fell behind the Shadow and Iron courtains who gave a ran to anyone for their money and nor Grozny neither Baba Yaga were fans of the modern world and literally grabbed the area by its balls and dragged back to the dark ages in a sense or farther and like the Soviet Union's their shadow still lingers and effects Ukraine (Piotr Krezhinsky, Darvag's Progeny for example worked on <i>Biopreparat</i>, a Soviet biological weapons research, where he and his subordinates tried to find a way to isolate the residue of the Tzimisce Antediluvian from their blood, as well as create bacteria and viruses that could be used to ghoul someone or bring sickness upon other Kindred. After World War II, he joined the Oradea league not the Sabbat, but you can immagine what he might left behind...)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So if your players are okay with it?<br /> Sure, go ahead, explore with a deep dive<br /> But even with WoD standards those games will be depressing, thats for sure<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-15-2025, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-16T07:03:28-07:00","id":1554388,"title":"","content":"I agree with Shadeprowler sayed, and to a little contribution, do a lot of research about the real world geopolitics in the conflict area. Turn this in a opportunitty to learn more about what is really happen and what is tell to us what is happen for both side of the war. I also recommend read the charnnel house europe, maybe someone here going to discorde with me (no problem) but I think it's a rpg book which present the influences from real conflict in the wod in a rspectfull way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-16T14:36:01-07:00","id":1554395,"title":"","content":"I've been following the war a lot actually. I am aware of how it's negatively affecting the Russian economy as there's a fuel shortage. Russian Soldiers are extremely low on supplies being on the brink of starvation and using tampons as gauze while mounting cavalry charges on horseback due to a lack of Vehicles. Putin is throwing soldiers into a meatgrinder as cannon fodder. There's a shortage of manpower so Putin duped Africans into fighting Ukraine, there's Chinese, North Koreans, Cubans and even people from Iran fighting for Russia. Putin is even using convicts for manpower in the war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 10-16-2025, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-16T14:39:16-07:00","id":1554396,"title":"","content":"On the World of Darkness side of things I'm aware of a Shadow Lord caern in Ukraine and a Black Spiral Dancer Hive in Chernobyl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-16T22:24:19-07:00","id":1554398,"title":"","content":"War is always two sided<br /> While the Russians have their problems - and thread craefully here, this is not the place for veiled political discussions ; that is why we told you talk it over with your players. Just as the players could be uncomfortable with things, forum visiters could be too - Ukraine have its fair share of attoricites and crimes, not just Russia<br /> Again, War - the situation is just like any other War this one is just in the spotlight at the moment<br /> Pair that with the fact prrior to the War, Ukraine was something that was called a &quot;Failed State&quot; - just try mention the Pandora Papers for example and see how quickly things escalate<br /> Also, Ukraine was - and arguably still is - in the top five or three most <i>corrupt</i> European states<br /> Also also, the issue of neo-Nazi military units is quite problematic, this only occurs because Ukrainian society in general doesn't see these units as &quot;bad&quot;, quite the contrary they are seen as defenders of Ukraine - worth noting that the neo-nazis are so prevalent because of lingering anti-soviet sentiment dating back generations<br /> And this is just scratching the surface - still enough for even the Wyrm to turn its head with disgust <br /> <br /> Again, as I said,<br /> Does it have lore and story potential?<br /> Yes<br /> Do you have to treat it very carefully?<br /> Yes<br /> Does it fundamentally different than any other conflict in the area or those conflicts already happening in the world?<br /> Not that much\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> You have to treat this very very very carefully, talk it through with your group, making sure everyone is okay with it and only then you should get involved<br /> Same with the Forum, mind you, such question is a very loaded gun, but we are all adults here, can handle this<br /> Still, there are subjects one must not poke unless absolutely necesaryy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T03:46:33-07:00","id":1554413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1554363-the-war-in-ukraine-has-surprising-potential-for-lore?p=1554388#post1554388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Shadeprowler sayed, and to a little contribution, do a lot of research about the real world geopolitics in the conflict area. Turn this in a opportunitty to learn more about what is really happen and what is tell to us what is happen for both side of the war.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that learning those things isn't really straightforward. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, a lot of things will be clear only in the future. And even with things we already know, perspective can change things <b>a lot</b>. Something as simple as your choice of sources or your Google algorithm can change drastically your understanding of the conflict even before your personal political views and cultural bias are added.<br /> <br /> It's usually far, far easier to <b><u>think</u></b> you know exactly what's going on than to actually know it.<br /> <br /> And while I think in the end it's ok both to apply real world politics with your bias in your own game, and to discuss politics in the forums, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> said it requires a lot of caution. For all we know we may have even soldiers from both sides as forum users here reading this, and they deserve the same respect as any other user. Overall avoiding veiled political discussion is good. If you want to be political, do it openly, and open to criticism. It is also good to avoid assuming things are self-evident, this is usually more a sign of our own bias than things being really certain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T05:26:14-07:00","id":1554417,"title":"","content":"To riff a bit off the last two posts:<br /> <br /> Ukraine is simultaneously exceptionally corrupt in comparison to other European countries, and middle-of-the-road corrupt in comparison to former Soviet states. Ukraine and the former Soviet bloc countries are also broadly in the same &quot;corruption&quot; bracket as most nations that only gained fully independence from European colonialism/imperialism in the 20th century.<br /> <br /> It's very hard to tell a story about (even if just in part) corruption in Ukraine (or any other country really) without inherently favoring a lens on how to view that corruption. <br /> <br /> In the specific context of WtA... how you frame corruption, and thus how you frame the Wyrm, matters a lot. As many fans of the game that still have a very complex relationship with it will tell you, the game has generally sucked at handling this in the books. How and why the Wyrm has become powerful in a given area in the official canon is hard to swallow as not being extremely biased (nobody at the original WW made sure to put a Hive at Three Mile Island or Windscale, which makes the very explicit point of a Hive at Chernobyl a statement even if an unintended one).<br /> <br /> In many ways WtA makes it harder than other games might in terms of setting games in real world conflict zones: the metaphysical nature of WtA's animist assumptions means you have to put reasons to things that in other games you could leave more ambiguous. Sure, &quot;there's a war, so there's more bane activity,&quot; is simple enough. But wars don't happen in a vacuum. Whenever you pick this Wyrm influenced faction is a major player on this side of the conflict, and this aspect of the Wyrm is endemic in the home territory of this side of a conflict, you're saying a lot of extra things about the real world conflict in trying to flesh out the things that mostly exist to get killed by the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T19:46:50-07:00","id":1554440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1554363-the-war-in-ukraine-has-surprising-potential-for-lore?p=1554398#post1554398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">War is always two sided<br /> While the Russians have their problems - and thread craefully here, this is not the place for veiled political discussions ; that is why we told you talk it over with your players. Just as the players could be uncomfortable with things, forum visiters could be too - Ukraine have its fair share of attoricites and crimes, not just Russia<br /> Again, War - the situation is just like any other War this one is just in the spotlight at the moment<br /> Pair that with the fact prrior to the War, Ukraine was something that was called a &quot;Failed State&quot; - just try mention the Pandora Papers for example and see how quickly things escalate<br /> Also, Ukraine was - and arguably still is - in the top five or three most <i>corrupt</i> European states<br /> Also also, the issue of neo-Nazi military units is quite problematic, this only occurs because Ukrainian society in general doesn't see these units as &quot;bad&quot;, quite the contrary they are seen as defenders of Ukraine - worth noting that the neo-nazis are so prevalent because of lingering anti-soviet sentiment dating back generations<br /> And this is just scratching the surface - still enough for even the Wyrm to turn its head with disgust<br /> <br /> Again, as I said,<br /> Does it have lore and story potential?<br /> Yes<br /> Do you have to treat it very carefully?<br /> Yes<br /> Does it fundamentally different than any other conflict in the area or those conflicts already happening in the world?<br /> Not that much<br /> <br /> You have to treat this very very very carefully, talk it through with your group, making sure everyone is okay with it and only then you should get involved<br /> Same with the Forum, mind you, such question is a very loaded gun, but we are all adults here, can handle this<br /> Still, there are subjects one must not poke unless absolutely necesaryy</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the neo-nazis aren't officially supported by the government, the Azov Batalion had it's neo-nazi elements removed. I also heard however that Ukrainian civilians had pretended to be friendly to Russian soldiers only to give them poisoned food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 10-17-2025, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T12:49:52-07:00","id":1554449,"title":"","content":"While I have my disagreements with Shadeprowler's assessments, I avoided getting into them because there's no real point to the debate right now. That there's a debate only highlights the caution of going down this road in a game everyone is expressing, and I chose to focus on the corruption point only because it's so easy to highlight the biases involved in how something gets framed even if a statement is largely agreed on as true or at least has a very strong case to be had for its truth if it's hard to establish more directly.<br /> <br /> &quot;I also heard...&quot; is a bad way to approach talking about an on-going war that you're considering moving into a fictional TTRPG game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T19:43:19-07:00","id":1554462,"title":"","content":"Well, anyways the Wyrm would try to stick it's tendrils wherever it can in both sides of the war. I also feel that vampires might try to exploit the conflict as well. The sudden and violent deaths caused by drone strikes could lead to the creation of Spectres on the Wraith side of things. But one thing is certain, the Russians are the bad guys in this war since they started it.","signature":"","edit